      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{5e89d0822aedbc56a3155d12|full_name} If they're hosting the world, they should have the right to feel safe in their own space. When a blocked person is still able to join, you'd still hear others talking to them, and you also get the awkward situation of \"oh, why can't you hear XYZ?\" and forcing them to talk about it before they're ready.\n\nThen with a younger audience, it's more likely to cause them unnecessary drama and similar. \n\nJust because it's \"silly\" doesn't mean it doesn't have its merits.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
